=== get on a project with no bendit.json
exit 0
--- stdout
off

=== show on a project with no bendit.json
exit 0
--- stdout
feature        | on/off | why
browser-driver | off    | (not set)
ux-design-laws | off    | (not set)
session-brief  | off    | (not set)
ls-guard       | off    | (not set)

=== set creates the file
exit 0
(silent)

=== get after set
exit 0
--- stdout
on

=== set off
exit 0
(silent)

=== get after set off
exit 0
--- stdout
off

=== set another feature
exit 0
(silent)

=== set an existing feature again (brief must survive)
exit 0
(silent)

=== show after merges
exit 0
--- stdout
feature        | on/off | why
browser-driver | off    | (not set)
ux-design-laws | on     | has UI
session-brief  | on     | still a git project
ls-guard       | on     | zsh

=== unknown feature
exit 2
--- stderr
features: <tmp>/bad/.claude/bendit.json: unknown feature 'lsguard' (known: browser-driver, ux-design-laws, session-brief, ls-guard)

=== on is not a bool
exit 2
--- stderr
features: <tmp>/bad/.claude/bendit.json: feature 'ls-guard': "on" must be true or false, got 'yes'

=== invalid JSON
exit 2
--- stderr
features: <tmp>/bad/.claude/bendit.json: not valid JSON: Expecting property name enclosed in double quotes: line 1 column 14 (char 13)

=== version is not 1
exit 2
--- stderr
features: <tmp>/bad/.claude/bendit.json: "version" must be 1, got 2

=== version missing
exit 2
--- stderr
features: <tmp>/bad/.claude/bendit.json: "version" must be 1, got None

=== why empty
exit 2
--- stderr
features: <tmp>/bad/.claude/bendit.json: feature 'ls-guard': "why" must be a non-empty string

=== an unknown key on a feature
exit 2
--- stderr
features: <tmp>/bad/.claude/bendit.json: feature 'ls-guard': unknown key 'brief'

=== top level is a list
exit 2
--- stderr
features: <tmp>/bad/.claude/bendit.json: top level must be an object

=== set refuses to overwrite a malformed file
exit 2
--- stderr
features: <tmp>/bad/.claude/bendit.json: top level must be an object

=== set unknown feature
exit 2
--- stderr
features: unknown feature 'lsguard' (known: browser-driver, ux-design-laws, session-brief, ls-guard)

=== no arguments
exit 2
--- stderr
usage: features.py get <root> <name> | set <root> <name> on|off <why> | show <root>

=== write into a read-only .claude
exit 2
--- stderr
features: <tmp>/ro/.claude/bendit.json: could not be written (the old file is untouched): Permission denied

